The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
static void *mall_get(struct tcf_proto *tp, u32 handle)
{
    return NULL;
}
```
Reason:
The `mall_get` function was implemented to always return `NULL`, which means it would never provide a valid filter, regardless of whether a matching filter handle existed. This resulted in the inability to retrieve any filter information, causing errors when users attempted to access filters.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
struct cls_mall_head *head = rtnl_dereference(tp->root);
if (head && head->handle == handle)
    return head;
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the `mall_get` function to first dereference the root of the filter tree and check if it exists and matches the requested handle. If a match is found, it returns the corresponding filter, allowing successful retrieval of filter information and resolving the issue of always returning `NULL`.

